Karl:

Can the below command to be rewritten to RETAIN only those ind below XO = 25

AND those ind above  XO =30?

The ind I am trying to EXCLUE has odd XO count that count falls into the XO 25-30 zone.

I need to keep the XO=zero individuals because they were not selectively genotyped

and I need retain both SG (and not SG) phenotypes for subsequent QTL analyses.

Unfortunately, I don’t know R well enough to make the below cmd do this.

Your help on this would be appreciated.

OBJNAME <- subset(OBJNAME, ind=(countXO(OBJNAME) < 100))

Jim

